{"slug":"centaurea-nigra","plant":{"taxon":"Centaurea nigra","family":"Asteraceae","rank":"species","gbif_key":3128225,"wikidata":"Q1851639","iucn":null,"gbif_occurrences":414171,"common_name":"common knapweed","names":[{"source":"culpeper","name":"Knapweed","monograph_id":"cul:170-knapweed","confidence":"medium","note":"Common knapweed; scaly heads, purple florets; slightly torn leaves could also suggest greater knapweed."}],"n_compounds":18,"top_compounds":[{"name":"beta-sitosterol","qid":"Q121802"},{"name":"lupeol","qid":"Q409366"},{"name":"stigmasterol","qid":"Q425004"},{"name":"α-amyrin","qid":"Q2501558"},{"name":"campesterol","qid":"Q2756479"},{"name":"matairesinol","qid":"Q4284467"},{"name":"(-)-arctigenin","qid":"Q4787603"},{"name":"arctiin","qid":"Q4787606"}],"epmc_total":28,"trials":0,"claims":[{"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","dsc":0,"cul":2,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.96,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"wounds","dsc":0,"cul":2,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.68,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"bruises","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.9,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"cancer","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.15,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"common_cold","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.9,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"diarrhea","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.84,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"hemorrhage","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.58,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"itch_scabies","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.95,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"nosebleed","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.99,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"sore_throat","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.97,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"}],"lead_score":null},"texts":{"cul:170-knapweed":{"ref":"Culpeper, Complete Herbal: Knapweed","headword":"Knapweed","lang":"en","source":"culpeper","text":"Saturn challenges the herb for his own. This Knapweed helps to stay fluxes, both of blood at the mouth or nose, or other outward parts, and those veins that are inwardly broken, or inward wounds, as also the fluxes of the belly; it stays distillation of thin and sharp humours from the head upon the stomach and lungs; it is good for those that are bruised by any fall, blows or otherwise, and is profitable for those that are bursten, and have ruptures, by drinking the decoction of the herb and roots in wine, and applying the same outwardly to the place. It is singularly good in all running sores, cancerous and fistulous, drying up of the moisture, and healing them up so gently, without sharpness; it doth the like to running sores or scabs of the head or other parts. It is of special use for the soreness of the throat, swelling of the uvula and jaws, and excellently good to stay bleeding, and heal up all green wounds.","spans":[{"start":84,"end":110,"concept_id":"nosebleed","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":188,"end":194,"concept_id":"wounds","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":208,"end":227,"concept_id":"diarrhea","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":238,"end":250,"concept_id":"common_cold","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":340,"end":356,"concept_id":"bruises","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":595,"end":600,"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":602,"end":611,"concept_id":"cancer","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":616,"end":625,"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":732,"end":737,"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":741,"end":746,"concept_id":"itch_scabies","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":804,"end":826,"concept_id":"sore_throat","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":844,"end":849,"concept_id":"sore_throat","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":889,"end":897,"concept_id":"h